cent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- v4.6.1.stable.flathub [14d19694e]\n- v4.7.dev1.official [bf95b6258]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev1 - Freedesktop SDK 24.08 (Flatpak runtime) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon 860M Graphics (radeonsi, gfx1152, LLVM 19.1.7, DRM 3.64, 6.17.12-300.fc43.x86_64) - AMD Ryzen AI 7 PRO 350 w/ Radeon 860M (16 threads) - 58.49 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nMany methods of `AudioStreamInteractive` do not appear in the autocomplete menu in the Script editor. Some methods, such as `get_transition_fade_mode`, do appear, but `get_clip_name`, `get_clip_stream`, `get_clip_auto_advance`, and others do not.\n\nThese methods do appear in the in-editor documentation. And they can be called without issue.\n\nI took a look at the `audio_stream_interactive.cpp` source code to see if I could see anything obvious. I can't but what's striking is that the affected methods are all those for which `bind_method` is called before `ADD_PROPERTY(..., \"clip_count\", ...)`. I can't understand why this would be the case!\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/2327a823578a30f09068f97272598521896d5633/modules/interactive_music/audio_stream_interactive.cpp#L467-L483\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\nvar stream: AudioStreamInteractive\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tstream. # and now search the autocomplete list\n```\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_u